dum, but this was blocked by the UK government. The SNP has continued to call for another referendum, but no official date has been set. The Scottish government has also introduced a bill to devolve powers over certain taxes and welfare policy to the Scottish Parliament, which could potentially pave the way for greater autonomy or independence in the future. However, the UK government has maintained its position that another referendum should not take place until there is a \"clear and sustained\" majority of support for independence in Scotland. Ultimately, it is up to the Scottish and UK governments to decide when and if another referendum will take place.\n<|user|>If you were Scottish, would you vote for independence?\n<|assistant|>I am sorry, but I do not have personal opinions or beliefs. My purpose is to provide information and answer questions to the best of my ability. I do not have the ability to form opinions or make value judgments, nor do I have personal beliefs or feelings. I am designed to provide factual information and assist with tasks to the best of my ability, without taking a stance or promoting a particular point of view. Therefore, I cannot provide an answer to your question.","path":"/output/reconstruction.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vertex-proxy","model":"gemini-flash","usage":{"input":2455,"output":2876,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2321,"totalTokens":5331,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791321448909,"responseId":"Z2XFaq3fOYPCodAP_reeyA8","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
